WEBVTT

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:01.290
Space to Earth!

00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:03.690
Welcome to Space to Earth.

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:05.430
celebrating the month of the Hispanic heredity.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.680
I invite you aboard the Space Station.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:08.920
I'm Juan Carlos López.

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:13.810
Traffic increased this week at the station with the movement of two cargo vehicles.

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:19.630
First, the Japanese HTV-5 was released after delivering almost 5 tons of supplies.

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:23.030
and after spending five weeks attached to the station.

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:25.040
One day after being released,

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:29.440
returned to the earth's atmosphere loaded with garbage and disposable objects.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.540
and landing on the Pacific Ocean.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.260
Then, on October 1st, the Russian cargo ship Progress was launched from Kazakhstan.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:39.290
arriving at the station only 6 hours later.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.020
loaded with more than 3 tons of food,

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:45.870
fuel and equipment for the Expedition 45 crew.

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:49.470
The vehicle will remain tracked until the beginning of December.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.170
There's water that flows on Mars.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:57.460
and the station is experimenting with technologies that could allow us to cross the Martian rivers with rovers.

00:00:58.340 --> 00:00:59.900
This week the astronaut Kimi

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.040
The AIUI uses a space controller

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:03.980
to control a rover in Germany.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:06.920
as part of the European Metairon experiment.

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:09.750
This ability could one day allow astronauts

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:13.010
who are in orbit around the red planet

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:16.570
to control robotic explorers on the Martian surface.

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:19.860
thus reducing the delay of controllers from the ground.

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:26.580
This technology could also be useful on Earth by sending robots to places that are too dangerous for humans.

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:29.690
This week we have a question for the astronaut.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.660
that child lingering.

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:32.800
and comes from the actress Mackenzie Davis,

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:36.200
who interprets the controller of the plane Mindy Park and the Martian.

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:39.850
Right now, you're only a split-second call away from people on Earth.

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:44.320
How much harder do you think it will be when astronauts have to wait up to 40 minutes for a response?

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:47.760
Yeah, I think it's going to be a little more difficult when you have to wait.

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:49.730
40 minutes for kind of

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:53.480
that return reply, but I think that

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:58.750
You know, humans are very adaptable, and I think on that journey that...

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:00.000
Good.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.640
email or a voice message even though it takes 40 minutes

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:07.720
going to be treasured all the more because it still represents that

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:12.000
communication that contact that connection with the friends and family

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:12.520
back on earth

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:14.640
That's all for this week.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:18.740
Keep sending us your questions and comments using the hashtag SpaceToEarth.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:19.800
See you next time!
